venv/
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
outputs/
.cache/
data/raw/*
# A `!` negation can't reach into a directory excluded by the pattern above unless
# the directory itself is re-included first — hence the un-ignore/re-ignore/
# un-ignore cascade below (see: git history "Force add test_results.csv", which
# worked around this same gitignore limitation instead of fixing it).
!data/raw/team-stats/
data/raw/team-stats/*
!data/raw/team-stats/team-records.csv
!data/raw/master-stats/
data/raw/master-stats/*
!data/raw/master-stats/test_results.csv
!data/raw/master-stats/model_metadata.json
!data/raw/master-stats/master_df.csv
# Same cascade, same reason — backend/outputs/ is otherwise a gitignored build
# artifact directory (line 4 above), but these three files are now written by
# .github/workflows/refresh-nba-data.yml and committed as source of truth for
# the API to read (Step 3 of the NBA.com connectivity fix — Render's network
# can't reach stats.nba.com, see backend/AGENTS.md's "Player ratings: refresh
# strategy"). Every other file under backend/outputs/ stays ignored.
!backend/outputs/
backend/outputs/*
!backend/outputs/player_power_rankings.json
!backend/outputs/team_style.json
!backend/outputs/player_projections.json
